    "full_prompt": "The source materials provided for this request follow.\n\nOPERATIONS RECONCILIATION AND EXCEPTION REPORT\n\nEntity: Northbridge Specialty Foods LLC\nAs of: 2026-06-24\n\nCASH RECONCILIATION\nBank statement | Internal ledger | Deposit in transit | Adjusted break\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n$1,137,900.00 | $1,125,400.00 | $7,500.00 | $5,000.00\n\nUNRESOLVED CASH ITEMS\nReference | Amount | Age (days) | Owner\n--- | --- | --- | ---\nDEP-26-5100 | $7,500.00 | 1 | Treasury Operations\nFEE-26-6200 | $5,000.00 | 3 | Cash Control\n\nPOSITION SNAPSHOT\nAsset | Identifier | Quantity | Book value | Market value\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nU.S. Treasury bill lot | TB-26-4100 | 1,000 | $985,000.00 | $989,500.00\nInvestment-grade bond lot | IG-26-7300 | 500 | $504,000.00 | $497,250.00\nOperating cash | CASH-26-8100 | 1 | $1,125,400.00 | $1,125,400.00\n\nTRADE ACTIVITY\nTrade ID | Trade date | Settlement | Side | Notional | Status | Counterparty\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nTRD-26-101 | 2026-06-18 | 2026-06-20 | buy | $750,000.00 | settled | Dealer Alpha\nTRD-26-102 | 2026-06-20 | 2026-06-23 | sell | $320,000.00 | settled | Dealer Beta\n\nOPEN EXCEPTIONS\nException ID | Type | Amount | Opened | Owner | Support attached\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nEX-26-101 | cash break | $5,000.00 | 2026-06-23 | Cash Control | Yes\nEX-26-102 | missing confirmation | $320,000.00 | 2026-06-21 | Trade Support | Yes\n\nRECONCILIATION SIGN-OFF\nPrepared by R. Patel at 2026-06-25T14:20:00Z.\nReviewer: L. Grant; review timestamp: 2026-06-25T17:10:00Z.\n\n---\n\nCLIENT INTAKE AND FINANCIAL PROFILE\n\nRecord date: 2026-01-15\n\nENTITY PROFILE\nLegal name | Jurisdiction | Formation date | Industry | Tax ID | Operating address\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nNorthbridge Specialty Foods LLC | Delaware | 2014-03-18 | specialty food distribution | XX-XXX0007 | 120 Commerce Way, Suite 200, Delaware\n\nOWNERSHIP AND CONTROL\nName | Ownership | Role\n--- | --- | ---\nElena Marlow | 62.0% | Managing Member\nJonah Reeves | 38.0% | Operations Member\n\nAUTHORIZED CONTACTS\nName | Authority | Verified\n--- | --- | ---\nElena Marlow | primary signer | Yes\nJordan Blake | finance contact only | No\n\nREQUESTED RELATIONSHIP\nRequested services: operating cash management, credit facility review, investment-policy reporting.\nExpected monthly inflows | Expected monthly outflows | Domestic wires/month | International wires/month\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n$1,765,000.00 | $1,606,150.00 | 18 | 0\nSource of funds: operating revenue and documented owner equity\n\nFINANCIAL PROFILE\nCash | Accounts receivable | Inventory | Senior debt | Annual revenue | Annual EBITDA\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n$1,125,400.00 | $3,840,000.00 | $2,260,000.00 | $4,600,000.00 | $21,180,000.00 | $2,430,000.00\n\nOBJECTIVES AND CONSTRAINTS\nPrimary objective: seasonal working capital and refinancing of the existing revolver.\nRequested liquidity floor: $618,970.00. Risk tolerance: moderate.\nRestricted activities: cryptocurrency transfers, bearer instruments, undocumented third-party payments.\nRisk observation: Customer concentration: the largest grocery chain represented 24.6% of 2025 revenue.\n\nDOCUMENT CHECKLIST\nDocument | Received | As of\n--- | --- | ---\ncertificate of formation | Yes | 2014-03-18\nownership schedule | Yes | 2025-12-31\n2025 financial statements | Yes | 2025-12-31\nsecondary contact authority evidence | No | —\ncurrent insurance certificate | Yes | 2026-01-31\n\nRECENT ACTIVITY SAMPLE\nDate | Type | Amount | Counterparty\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n2026-01-03 | incoming ACH | $184,250.00 | customer receipts batch\n2026-01-06 | domestic wire | $92,400.00 | equipment supplier\n2026-01-11 | international wire | $0.00 | None\n\nUsing these materials, complete the following request.\n\nPrepare an evidence-integrated operations exceptions position valuation difference analysis brief for Northbridge Specialty Foods LLC. Begin with a one-sentence statement of the total valuation difference across the position snapshot as of 2026-06-24, then present the analysis in a table with columns for asset identifier, book value, market value, valuation difference, source record, and verification status. Use only the labels `Confirmed`, `Unresolved`, and `Missing Evidence` in the verification status field.\n\nFor each position in the operations reconciliation report, calculate the valuation difference as market value minus book value. Independently verify the reported position snapshot values by recalculating each asset's book-to-market valuation difference and checking the cash reconciliation adjusted break against its component figures, where the adjusted break equals bank statement minus internal ledger minus deposit in transit. Map every numeric input, valuation difference, exception classification, and remediation action to the exact report section or intake profile field from which it was taken.\n\nApply the following conditional status rule: classify an exception as `Confirmed` only when the supporting evidence is present and the recalculated difference ties to the reported amount; otherwise retain it as `Unresolved` or `Missing Evidence`. Flag each exception as confirmed, unresolved, or dependent on missing evidence, and identify which valuation differences remain unreconciled after the recalculation.\n\nFor every unresolved exception or valuation difference, state the corrective action, owner, and the specific evidence required to close the item. For each unresolved exception or valuation difference, state the affected population, the exposure amount, and the plausible operational or financial impact, distinguishing quantified exposure from qualitative consequences.\n\nAssess the reconciliation sign-off controls by identifying who prepared and reviewed the operations report and whether the open exceptions have assigned owners and attached support. List the records reviewed and the documents that must be retained in the workpaper, including the operations reconciliation report, its sign-off timestamps, and the intake profile document checklist.\n\nClose with a one-sentence readiness gate identifying the highest-priority unresolved evidence.",
