    "full_prompt": "The source materials provided for this request follow.\n\nEntity: THE BOEING COMPANY\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 138,552,000,000 | 137,100,000,000 | 137,012,000,000 | 156,363,000,000 | 168,235,000,000\nLiabilities | 153,398,000,000 | 152,948,000,000 | 154,240,000,000 | 160,277,000,000 | 162,778,000,000\nStockholdersEquity | -14,999,000,000 | -15,883,000,000 | -17,233,000,000 | -3,908,000,000 | 5,454,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 108,666,000,000 | 109,523,000,000 | 109,275,000,000 | 127,998,000,000 | 128,459,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 81,992,000,000 | 90,052,000,000 | 95,827,000,000 | 97,078,000,000 | 108,115,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 8,052,000,000 | 14,614,000,000 | 12,691,000,000 | 13,801,000,000 | 10,921,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 2,641,000,000 | 2,517,000,000 | 2,649,000,000 | 2,631,000,000 | 2,921,000,000\nLongTermDebt | 57,921,000,000 | 56,794,000,000 | 52,055,000,000 | 53,625,000,000 | 53,848,000,000\nOtherLiabilitiesNoncurrent | 1,750,000,000 | 2,211,000,000 | 2,332,000,000 | 2,318,000,000 | 2,432,000,000\n\n---\n\nEntity: THE BOEING COMPANY\nINCOME STATEMENT (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nRevenues | 62,286,000,000 | 66,608,000,000 | 77,794,000,000 | 66,517,000,000 | 89,463,000,000\nCostOfRevenue | 59,237,000,000 | 63,078,000,000 | 70,070,000,000 | 68,508,000,000 | 85,174,000,000\nGrossProfit | 3,049,000,000 | 3,530,000,000 | 7,724,000,000 | -1,991,000,000 | 4,289,000,000\nOperatingIncomeLoss | -2,870,000,000 | -3,519,000,000 | -773,000,000 | -10,707,000,000 | 4,281,000,000\nNetIncomeLoss | -4,202,000,000 | -4,935,000,000 | -2,222,000,000 | -11,817,000,000 | 2,235,000,000\nIncomeTaxExpenseBenefit | -743,000,000 | 31,000,000 | 237,000,000 | -381,000,000 | 397,000,000\nResearchAndDevelopmentExpense | 2,249,000,000 | 2,852,000,000 | 3,377,000,000 | 3,812,000,000 | 3,615,000,000\nEarningsPerShareBasic (USD/shares) | -7.15 | -8.3 | -3.67 | -18.36 | 2.49\n\nUsing these materials, complete the following request.\n\nProduce a research evidence table specification for THE BOEING COMPANY's financials that supports an integrated cross-statement analysis of the supplied balance sheet and income statement annual 10-K values. The specification must define every column, row grouping, source mapping, calculation, and status rule needed to build the table, but it must not fill in the table or state the final results.\n\nUse only the two supplied statement materials: the balance sheet and the income statement, both reported for THE BOEING COMPANY at the fiscal-year endpoints 2021-12-31, 2022-12-31, 2023-12-31, 2024-12-31, and 2025-12-31. Preserve the exact entity name, statement labels, concept names, fiscal-year endpoints, USD units, signs, and as-reported values wherever they are carried into the specification or used in any calculation. Apply the five balance-sheet fiscal-year endpoints consistently as the only valid reporting windows, and require the table to flag any concept row that does not have a value for one of those endpoints as missing rather than carrying forward or estimating it.\n\nRequire an independent recalculation of each reported income-statement subtotal and derived per-share figure from the underlying reported components, with a column showing the recalculated value, the variance from the as-reported figure, and a tie-out status for each fiscal year. Require an Evidence column that maps every input, calculated result, tie-out status, and missing-value flag to the exact statement, concept row, and fiscal-year column from which it was taken.\n\nRequire the specification to define a cross-statement ratio for each fiscal year that uses an income-statement flow as the numerator and a balance-sheet stock as the denominator, with the exact concept names, units, sign treatment, and rounding or precision rule stated for each operand. Use only Pass, Fail, and Missing Evidence in the tie-out status field.\n\nBegin with a one-sentence statement of the table's analytical purpose. Close with a Next action: line that states the one unresolved cross-statement item that must still be resolved before the table can be considered complete. Mark any requested field, cross-statement relationship, or derived figure that cannot be established from the two supplied materials as Not Determinable.",
