    "full_prompt": "The source material provided for this request follows.\n\nSBA 7(a) Borrower Information Form OMB Control No.: 3245-0348\nFor use with all SBA 7(a) Loan Programs Expiration Date: 6/30/2027\nSBA Form 191\n9 (02/2025) 1 \nApplicant Business Legal Name (OC □ EPC□): \nOperating Business Legal Name (OC): \nDBA or Tradename (if applicable) \nBusiness TIN (EIN, SSN) \nPrimary Industry / NAICS Code (6 digit): Business Phone: \nUnique Entity ID used in SAM.gov, if any Year began operations: \nEntity Type \nCheck One: \n□ Sole proprietor\n□ Partnership\n□ C-Corp\n□ S-Corp\n□ LLC\n□ Other ______________________\nSpecial Ownership Type \n(Select all that apply): \n□ Employee Stock Ownership Plan (ESOP)\n□ 401(k) or ROBS 401(k) Trust\n□ Cooperative\n□ Native-American Tribal-Owned Business\n□ Other __________________________\nBusiness Address (Street, City, State, Zip Code) \nDo not use P.O. Box address \nProject Address, if different than Business Address \n(Street, City, State, Zip Code) Do not use P.O. Box address \nPrimary Contact Name \nPrimary Contact Email Address \n# of existing employees (including owners, all part-time, full-time and all employees of domestic and foreign \nAffiliates – do not convert to FTE) \n# of FTE jobs saved/retained because of the loan (including owners) \n# of new FTE jobs created because of the loan (including owners) \nPurpose of the loan (i.e., Purchase Real Estate; Construction; Equipment; Inventory; Eligible Debt Refinancing; Working Capital; etc.) \n□ Acquisition/installation of equipment $ . □ Purchase/Construction of Commercial Real Estate $ . \n□ Working Capital $ . □ Acquisition of inventory $ . \n□ Business acquisition (Change of Ownership) $ . □ Debt refinancing $ . \n□ Other: $ . □ Other: $ . \nApplicant Ownership (Mandatory) and Demographic Information – Identify all entities that own at least 20% of the Applicant, including the \nnatural persons who own those entities, and at least 51% of the Beneficial Owners (as defined in SOP 50 10) of the Applicant. Attach a separate \nsheet if necessary. \nOwner’s Legal Name \n(First name Last name) \nTitle Ownership % TIN (SSN/EIN) Home Address \n(Street, City, State, Zip Code - No P.O. Box)\n\nUsing this material, complete the following request.\n\nUsing solely the supplied Form 1919 excerpt, draft a prospective loan approval-condition matrix for our SBA 7(a) credit memo template. The excerpt is an uncompleted form rather than a borrower file. Scope the matrix to collection and review of the information shown; do not infer borrower-specific deficiencies, eligibility, creditworthiness, or approval. Any proposed preapproval gate must be identified as lender judgment rather than an SBA approval requirement.\n\nFocus on business and project addresses, loan purposes and their dollar fields, the three employment measures, and ownership disclosures. In every matrix row, provide the supporting field label or short quotation, the condition and its applicability trigger, the information needed to evaluate it, a prospective clearance or escalation test, and any limitation on what the excerpt establishes. Distinguish an express form instruction from a field that is merely presented for completion, and clearly label analyst-proposed checks or corroborating documents. State the current evidentiary status without treating blank fields as confirmed borrower failures.\n\nBuild the review logic as follows:\n- For addresses, preserve the address restrictions and the condition under which a separate project address is requested. Show how a future response would determine whether the additional address condition activates.\n- For employment, preserve the population and measurement basis of each field. Explain how a reviewer should handle entries prepared on an inconsistent basis without converting headcount to FTE or inventing a conversion method. The three measures must not be assumed capable of being added or reconciled to one another.\n- For loan purposes, map the purpose selections to their associated amount fields. Separate a proposed consistency check from any eligibility conclusion: a purpose label is not proof that the proposed use qualifies. Identify the limits on dollar reconciliation when neither completed amounts nor an independent loan-total comparison basis is supplied; do not calculate a total from blanks.\n- For ownership, preserve the exact disclosure thresholds and distinguish the entities covered, the natural persons behind those entities, and beneficial-owner coverage. Translate these into conditional review steps only as far as the excerpt permits. Identify where the referenced but unavailable SOP definition prevents a fully operational acceptance test. Preserve the separate-sheet condition without assuming that a sheet is always required or has been received.\n\nConclude with an approval-review handoff derived from the matrix: identify which conditions could be evaluated from future form responses, which may also require the expressly conditional attachment, and which depend on missing interpretive material or analyst-proposed corroboration. These groups may overlap. Tie each requested input to the condition it would help resolve, and distinguish unresolved source interpretation from missing applicant information. Explain the boundary between clearing these information conditions and making an actual loan approval decision; do not import requirements from other form pages or external SBA rules.",
