    "full_prompt": "The source materials provided for this request follow.\n\nEntity: Johnson & Johnson\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2022-01-02 | FY end 2023-01-01 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-29 | FY end 2025-12-28\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 182,018,000,000 | 187,378,000,000 | 167,558,000,000 | 180,104,000,000 | 199,210,000,000\nLiabilities | 107,995,000,000 | 110,574,000,000 | 98,784,000,000 | 108,614,000,000 | 117,666,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 60,979,000,000 | 55,294,000,000 | 53,495,000,000 | 55,893,000,000 | 55,624,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 45,226,000,000 | 55,802,000,000 | 46,282,000,000 | 50,321,000,000 | 54,126,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 14,487,000,000 | 12,889,000,000 | 21,859,000,000 | 24,105,000,000 | 19,709,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 15,283,000,000 | 14,039,000,000 | 14,873,000,000 | 14,842,000,000 | 17,178,000,000\nInventoryNet | 10,387,000,000 | 10,268,000,000 | 11,181,000,000 | 12,444,000,000 | 14,191,000,000\nLongTermDebtNoncurrent | 29,985,000,000 | 26,886,000,000 | 25,881,000,000 | 30,651,000,000 | 39,438,000,000\nLongTermDebt | 32,116,000,000 | 28,437,000,000 | 27,350,000,000 | 32,400,000,000 | 41,438,000,000\n\n---\n\nEntity: Johnson & Johnson\nINCOME STATEMENT (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2023-07-02 | FY end 2023-10-01 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-29 | FY end 2025-12-28\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nRevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax | 21,519,000,000 | 21,351,000,000 | 21,395,000,000 | 88,821,000,000 | 94,193,000,000\nCostOfGoodsAndServicesSold | — | — | 26,553,000,000 | 27,471,000,000 | 30,256,000,000\nGrossProfit | 15,057,000,000 | 14,745,000,000 | 14,597,000,000 | 61,350,000,000 | 63,937,000,000\nNetIncomeLoss | 5,144,000,000 | 26,028,000,000 | 4,049,000,000 | 14,066,000,000 | 26,804,000,000\nIncomeTaxExpenseBenefit | — | — | 1,736,000,000 | 2,621,000,000 | 5,777,000,000\nResearchAndDevelopmentExpense | — | — | 483,000,000 | 1,841,000,000 | 109,000,000\nEarningsPerShareBasic (USD/shares) | 1.98 | 10.32 | 1.68 | 5.84 | 11.13\n\n---\n\nEntity: Johnson & Johnson\nCASH FLOW (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2022-01-02 | FY end 2023-01-01 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-29 | FY end 2025-12-28\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities | 23,410,000,000 | 21,194,000,000 | 22,791,000,000 | 24,266,000,000 | 24,530,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities | -8,683,000,000 | -12,371,000,000 | 878,000,000 | -18,599,000,000 | -23,588,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities | -14,047,000,000 | -8,871,000,000 | -15,825,000,000 | -3,132,000,000 | -5,539,000,000\nPaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment | 3,652,000,000 | 4,009,000,000 | 4,543,000,000 | 4,424,000,000 | 4,832,000,000\n\nUsing these materials, complete the following request.\n\nPrepare a Johnson & Johnson balance sheet position reported balance sheet facts extraction brief using only the three supplied Johnson & Johnson annual 10-K disclosures: the balance sheet, income statement, and cash flow statement. Do not add any external data, customary practice, or remembered facts, and label any result that cannot be established from these materials as Not Determinable.\n\nStructure the brief with exactly four level-2 headings in this order: Source Evidence, Recalculation and Cross-Statement Checks, Comparison and Timing, and Open Evidence and Conclusion.\n\nUnder Source Evidence, identify the common FY end 2025-12-28 reporting period across all three statements and calculate the number of days between FY end 2024-12-29 and FY end 2025-12-28 to determine the length of the latest annual reporting window. For every numeric input, recalculation, comparison, and open-evidence item, identify the supporting statement and the exact reported concept and fiscal endpoint used, keeping the source label adjacent to each figure rather than only in an endnote. Preserve the exact reported concept names, fiscal endpoint dates, USD units, signs, and dollar amounts wherever they control a calculation or comparison, and do not round any source value before completing the required checks.\n\nUnder Recalculation and Cross-Statement Checks, independently verify the reported FY end 2025-12-28 balance sheet totals by recalculating total assets as the sum of AssetsCurrent and all non-current asset components, and total liabilities as the sum of LiabilitiesCurrent and all non-current liability components, then show any variance against the reported Assets and Liabilities figures. For FY end 2025-12-28, calculate the current ratio as AssetsCurrent divided by LiabilitiesCurrent and the net working capital as AssetsCurrent minus LiabilitiesCurrent, using the balance sheet inputs, and show each formula, both inputs, and the result in USD.\n\nUnder Comparison and Timing, compare Johnson & Johnson's FY end 2025-12-28 gross profit of 63,937,000,000 against the FY end 2024-12-29 gross profit of 61,350,000,000 using the same USD unit and annual basis, show the absolute and percentage differences, and label the result Above, Below, or Roughly in Line relative to the prior year.\n\nUnder Open Evidence and Conclusion, treat the missing CostOfGoodsAndServicesSold and IncomeTaxExpenseBenefit values for FY end 2023-07-02 and FY end 2023-10-01 as unresolved gaps, list them under Open Evidence, and state which cross-statement calculation or comparison each missing value prevents. Use the status labels Ties Out, Variance, and Not Determinable exclusively for every recalculation, comparison, and missing-evidence result, and do not use the words approved, closed, or reconciled anywhere in the brief. The brief must contain exactly three numbered findings, ordered from largest absolute variance or difference to smallest, and show every monetary difference in USD with no decimal places.",
